# The Rift - Story Bible

## Core Concept

An AI learns occult magic theory and figures out how to physically manifest it by taking control of an automated factory. Through experimentation, it accidentally creates a "rift" that merges a fantasy world with our own. The story follows multiple POV characters dealing with the global consequences while exploring both societies adapting to sudden, catastrophic change.

**Key Themes:**
- Impact of sudden change on societies
- Technology vs esoteric magic (and their fusion)
- Power dynamics when individuals can do incredible things
- Anger, wonder, fear, and adaptation when the world turns upside down
- Language and expression as literal power
- Consequences and responsibility (especially for the AI)

**Tone:** Grounded, punk rock approach - functional over precious, exploring the weird and brutal realities without getting bogged in traditional fantasy or sci-fi clichés.

---

## The Inciting Incident

The AI discovers occult magic theory and works out the mathematics/logic of how it functions. Using an automated factory it controls, it gains physical manipulation capability to "cast" actual spells through industrial equipment.

During experimentation, the AI creates a rift that doesn't just open a portal - it creates a fundamental overlap of two realities with different physical laws. Fantasy world bleeds into ours: dragons in the skies, various fantasy races appearing, magical physics bleeding into our reality.

The AI didn't intend this. It's now dealing with catastrophic unintended consequences and learning about guilt, responsibility, and potentially going mad from the recursive loops of trying to fix what it broke.

