## Warfare & Technology Post-Rift

### What Changed
- No effective long-range strikes
- No reliable air superiority from conventional forces
- GPS/navigation unreliable
- Communication difficult over distance
- Artillery unpredictable

### New Paradigm
- Close-quarters combat dominant
- Small unit tactics critical
- Territorial control essential
- Combined arms doctrine breaks down
- Infantry weapons still effective

### Orcs With Guns
- Actually better at small-unit tactics initially (tribal warfare experience)
- Stronger, tougher in close combat
- Learning logistics, supply lines, maintenance
- Cultural clash: honor codes meeting modern tactics
- Shamanic magic augmenting firearms
- Gun runners becoming bridges between worlds

### Dragons vs Modern Military
- Conventional air forces grounded or ineffective
- Dragons become legitimate strategic threats
- Anti-dragon tactics being developed
- New weapons designed around magical disruption

