## Societal Impact

### Collapse Points
- Food supply chains breaking
- Mass migration (both directions)
- New diseases (biological and magical)
- Religious upheaval (magic and gods are real)
- Economic collapse (what's gold worth when dragons hoard it?)

### Adaptation
- Both societies learning from each other
- Technology users learning magical principles
- Magic users adopting technology
- New hybrid approaches emerging
- Power structures in flux

### Human Scientists vs Magic
- Can measure effects but not mechanism
- Magic follows rules, just not physical laws
- Variables are: intent, symbolic correspondence, true names
- Some breakthroughs:
  - Fiber optic cable in specific pattern creates teleportation circle
  - Broadcasting on right frequency disrupts spells
  - Runes on circuit boards enhance technology
  - Red Bull gives fantasy beings scientific visions

