## Story Approach

### Avoid
- The "chosen one" trope
- Simple good vs evil
- Tech wins or magic wins scenarios
- Vendor lock-in to either worldview
- Over-explanation that kills wonder
- Cliché fantasy or sci-fi elements

### Embrace
- Multiple POV characters (Game of Thrones style)
- "Cursed with knowledge" - people understand different pieces, can't coordinate
- Opportunists on both sides
- Gray morality and difficult choices
- Absurdist elements (kazoo warfare) alongside serious consequences
- Punk rock philosophy: functional over perfect, build genuinely useful not feature-bloated

### Scale
- Global impact
- Focus on principal characters
- Multiple storylines and locations
- Large supporting cast
- Show both sides adapting

